From: ACK72 <ACK72@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] luci-base: do not instantiate a missing wireless device

SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0

A disabled or transitioning wireless interface may have neither a runtime
ifname nor a synthetic network ID (for example, a list-valued device option
from wifi-scripts). WifiNetwork.getDevice() must return null in that case,
as its caller isUp() already expects. Constructing Device(undefined) reaches
Device.getType() and throws at this.device.indexOf(), breaking the entire
wireless page even while rpcd and the driver remain responsive.

Keep valid runtime and synthetic interface names unchanged.

---
--- a/modules/luci-base/htdocs/luci-static/resources/network.js
+++ b/modules/luci-base/htdocs/luci-static/resources/network.js
@@ -4485,7 +4485,8 @@
 	 * device associated with this wireless network.
 	 */
 	getDevice() {
-		return Network.prototype.instantiateDevice(this.getIfname());
+		const ifname = this.getIfname();
+		return (ifname != null ? Network.prototype.instantiateDevice(ifname) : null);
 	},
 
 	/**
